WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.850
Netflix is a vast sea of entertainment options.

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:06.880
So many, in fact, that you may feel like you're
drowning in possibilities.

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:07.880
We get it.

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:10.710
It can overwhelm even the most experienced
binge watcher.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:11.710
But don't worry.

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:16.299
Because we're here to throw you a cinematic
lifeline with underappreciated gems on Netflix

00:00:16.299 --> 00:00:18.490
that you just have to watch.

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:20.609
Moonrise Kingdom

00:00:20.609 --> 00:00:25.590
Described as an "eccentric, pubescent love
story" by The Hollywood Reporter, Moonrise

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:30.300
Kingdom is definitely the most romantic movie
on director Wes Anderson's resumé.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:35.690
This coming-of-age tale has a great cast,
including Tilda Swinton, Bruce Willis, Edward

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:37.000
Norton, and Bill Murray.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:39.120
"I'll be out back.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:42.820
I'm gonna find a tree to chop down."

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:51.920
And it also boasts a beautiful setting as
well as all the quirky hallmarks that Anderson

00:00:51.929 --> 00:00:53.730
fans have come to love.

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:55.969
Nightcrawler

00:00:55.969 --> 00:01:01.730
Suspenseful and visually stunning, this Oscar-nominated
thriller features Jake Gyllenhaal in a creepily

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:06.890
convincing performance as a sociopathic freelance
videographer tasked with covering the late-night

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:08.860
crime beat for local news stations.

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:14.939
"We find our viewers are more interested in
urban crime creeping into the suburbs.

00:01:14.939 --> 00:01:19.250
What that means is a victim or victims preferably
well off and white."

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:23.760
The performance landed Gyllenhaal a Golden
Globe nomination for best Actor, while the

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:28.540
screenplay for Nightcrawler earned an Oscar
nomination for writer Dan Gilroy.

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:31.009
Tucker &amp; Dale vs. Evil

00:01:31.009 --> 00:01:35.649
The thing we love about Tucker &amp; Dale vs.
Evil is how it turns traditional horror tropes

00:01:35.649 --> 00:01:36.700
on their head.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:42.310
This comedy horror film stars Alan Tudyk and
Tyler Labine as a pair of West Virginia hillbillies

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:45.869
who encounter a group of clueless college
students on a camping trip.

00:01:45.869 --> 00:01:49.890
When one of the college students accidentally
hurts herself, the hillbillies take care of

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:54.500
her — until the misguided college kids attempt
to rescue her from what they assume are scary

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:55.950
backwoods hicks.

00:01:55.950 --> 00:02:00.799
All sorts of hilarious and horrific hijinks
ensue, which make this movie a perfect choice

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:01.860
for your Netflix queue.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:09.800
In Your Eyes

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:15.390
This Joss Whedon jam tells the story of two
very different people - a married socialite

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:20.200
from New Hampshire and an ex-con from New
Mexico - who have shared an inexplicable mental

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:23.210
connection since childhood that neither understands.

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:27.520
As the connection deepens, they realize they
aren't going crazy, because there actually

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:29.650
is another person inside their heads.

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:34.060
"I wake up, and you're not there.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:37.140
I call all my friends."

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:42.640
But while they know they're sane, the rest
of the world isn't so sure.

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:44.110
The Way Back

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:48.770
Based on a memoir by a former Polish prisoner
of war, The Way Back tells the incredible

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:54.790
story of a group of P.O.W.s who escape from
a Siberian gulag and walk over 4,000 miles,

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:59.320
crossing deserts and even the Himalayas in
an epic quest to find freedom.

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:01.900
"This changes everything."

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:05.680
"There's nowhere to hide."

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:11.409
It also features amazing cinematography as
well as a stellar cast including Colin Farrell

00:03:11.409 --> 00:03:15.470
and Oscar nominees Ed Harris and Saoirse Ronan.

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:17.340
Oldboy

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:22.349
While an American version of Oldboy directed
by Spike Lee was released in 2013, the original

00:03:22.349 --> 00:03:26.750
South Korean movie is far superior — and
it's on Netflix for your viewing pleasure.

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:31.879
Based on a Japanese manga, Oldboy is a thrilling
neo-noir mystery, centered on the story of

00:03:31.879 --> 00:03:36.470
a man who is abducted and held for 15 years
in a prison cell, with no knowledge of who

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:39.140
his captors are or why they are keeping him
there.

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:54.099
Then, he finds himself suddenly released and
given the chance to get revenge on his captors

00:03:54.099 --> 00:03:56.560
— if he can find them in a mere five days.

00:03:56.560 --> 00:04:02.170
And then… well, we can't say anything else
without spoiling the many shocks and surprises.

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:04.030
Kung Fury

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:09.000
Funded entirely by Kickstarter, Kung Fury
debuted at the Cannes film festival before

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:13.019
being released free of charge on YouTube,
where it gained such a cult following that

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:15.920
it secured international distribution on Netflix.

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:20.850
As crazy as that story is, though, it pales
in comparison to the utterly insane 80's action

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:23.460
parody mashup that unspools on your screen.

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:29.100
With everything from time-traveling demi-gods
to dinosaur cops to kung-fu Hitler, Kung Fury

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:32.880
delivers a knockout blow to your funny bone
that you may never recover from.

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:34.480
"Sorry I doubted you Triceracop.

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:37.270
You're the best damn partner I've ever had."

00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:40.320
"I came back in time for you, Kung Fury.

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:43.340
Because, damnit I love you."

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:45.890
These Final Hours

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:51.271
With only 12 hours left before an asteroid-induced
global firestorm reaches Australia, a dude

00:04:51.271 --> 00:04:56.340
named James abandons his pregnant girlfriend
in search of the ultimate apocalyptic party.

00:04:56.340 --> 00:05:00.890
Along the way, though, the self-indulgent
and arrogant James meets a young girl and

00:05:00.890 --> 00:05:05.430
discovers he has some serious choices to make
about how he truly wants to spend his last

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:06.650
moments on Earth.

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:08.700
"Forgive me then.

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:12.700
Forgive me, for what I'm gonna do."

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:19.230
Tense, edgy, and raw, These Final Hours shows
us the best and worst of humanity when pushed

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:20.230
to the brink.

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:24.380
Be prepared for an edge-of-your-seat ride
that will also inspire tears and deep thoughts

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:27.670
about what you would do if you only had 12
hours left to live.

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:31.340
Which is easy, just eat as much pizza as possible.

00:05:31.340 --> 00:05:32.810
Centurion

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:37.551
At first glance, Centurion looks like another
vanilla sword-and-sandals war epic, which

00:05:37.551 --> 00:05:41.910
is probably why it absolutely tanked at the
box office when it was released in 2010.

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:45.941
But it'd be a shame for any fan of bloody
action to pass on this hidden gem, because

00:05:45.941 --> 00:05:50.870
Centurion definitely delivers much more than
it promises, focusing on a tiny band of Roman

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:55.320
soldiers trapped in enemy territory as they
try to make their way home.

00:05:57.340 --> 00:05:58.480
"It's a trap!"

00:05:58.480 --> 00:05:59.500
"Fall back!

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:00.540
Fall back!"

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:07.200
Michael Fassbender leads the cast through
every blood-soaked battle, while Neil Marshall,

00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:12.380
who is best known for directing some of the
most popular episodes of Game of Thrones ever,

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:13.530
is behind the camera.

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:17.070
So sit back, relax, and watch a bunch of people
kill each other.

00:06:17.070 --> 00:06:19.810
What else are you going to do while you wait
for the next season of Thrones?

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:21.539
Thanks for watching!

00:06:21.539 --> 00:06:24.240
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:26.720
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

